@startuml
!theme plain
title D07 route LEZ status (LezStatus + derived STALE)

[*] --> UNCHECKED : route persisted without a ruleset\n(job without a snapshot)
[*] --> COMPLIANT : completion callback certifies\nwith the job's snapshot, no violation
[*] --> VIOLATION : completion callback certifies\nwith the job's snapshot, violations

UNCHECKED --> COMPLIANT : recheck / send guard / saved revision
UNCHECKED --> VIOLATION : recheck / send guard / saved revision
COMPLIANT --> VIOLATION : recheck or send guard\nwith the current rules
VIOLATION --> COMPLIANT : recheck after rules, permits\nor the plan changed

state STALE #EEEEEE : derived on read, never stored:\nstored lez_ruleset_hash differs from the\nhash of the current compilation
COMPLIANT -[dashed]-> STALE : rules changed since certification
VIOLATION -[dashed]-> STALE : rules changed since certification
STALE -[dashed]-> COMPLIANT : POST /compliance/recheck
STALE -[dashed]-> VIOLATION : POST /compliance/recheck

note bottom
  A route carries lez_status, lez_checked_at, lez_ruleset_hash and
  lez_violations (JSON). A 422 from the send guard still commits the
  VIOLATION verdict (noRollbackFor).
end note
@enduml
